// Free answers: prose or a proof, which the checker cannot decide. The attempt is
// logged first with the verdict pending (session_answer_item), so the reference
// answer is shown only after a committed attempt. session_route_free then asks
// the grader (grade_attempt) about it; a "graded" answer is written to the log as
// a graded line from the model, anything else (server unreachable, unsure, low
// confidence, a refusal) leaves the attempt pending and sends the learner to
// mark it themselves with session_self_grade, which writes the marks they give
// as a graded line from the learner. Nothing counts toward retention, the plan
// or the scoreboard until a verdict is logged. session_ungraded says whether the
// item on screen is still waiting for one, which is what stops `gym next`.

session_ungraded(Log_events session_events, string[] session_shown) {
  string session_escaped = log_escape(session_shown[(import session_slot_item)]);
  int session_waiting_at = log_pending_index(session_events, session_escaped, len(session_events.kinds));
  int session_waiting = session_shown[(import session_slot_state)] == "committed" && session_waiting_at >= 0;
} return int session_waiting;
